  "source_route": [
    "Read Federer pp. 279\u2013280 and the cited mixed-volume monotonicity before proof construction. The required original vertical-ball/ambient-ball coefficient comparison follows from existing scalar-row Fubini, exact weighted reflections and intrinsic isometry invariance. Independent evaluation laws precede a local finite polynomial evaluation inverse, using the existing internal root count and finite linear algebra. No general external mixed-volume monotonicity is assumed.",
    "An actual one-coordinate stretch t>=1 has intrinsic coefficients at most t times the original coefficients. Iterate the first coordinate block. Exact determinant transport normalizes the actual anisotropic Steiner polynomials. Their separately bounded coefficients have actual individual limits: compact Hausdorff volume continuity gives nodal convergence, and the finite inverse recovers the coefficients. This is not coefficientwise inference from pointwise ordered polynomials.",
    "Use the same finite evaluation inverse on the actual section Steiner polynomials. Original block Fubini, finite signed integration and coefficient unscaling identify ordinary section integrals. Empty and thin compact fibres retain their original coefficients. The coefficient comparison proves the compact section bound.",
    "Prove bounded convex sources Lebesgue measurable using the existing interior-or-null-closure split, original compact interior contractions, exact dilation volumes, dilation slack and measure completeness. Actual original open vertical-ball sums then give Fubini and ordinary integrability of the original nonclosed convex section functions. Fibre inclusion in compact source closure, original intrinsic order and exact gauge closure restore the original numerical bound without any false pointwise section-closure equality.",
    "The actual closed-convex Caratheodory construction extends the generator comparison to arbitrary targets. Keep source indices under section projection; total countable nonnegative integration and covering infima give every cutoff upper integral. Cofinal reciprocal cutoffs and the existing increasing upper-integral theorem give the literal all-set upper-star inequality without assuming section measurability.",
    "Apply the all-set section theorem to the actual Cartesian set. Its fibre mass is the second original mass times the sealed first-factor characteristic function. The existing extended characteristic integral evaluates the lower bound, and the already released Gillespie product upper theorem gives equality on exactly the ordinary partial-product domain. Four concrete regressions cover the R^0 atom, unit square, infinite second mass and undefined zero-times-infinity arithmetic."
  ],
  "coverage_qualification": "Together with the released continuity, corrected secant, sharp comparison and product upper results, the requested noncommentary 3.2.45 scope is complete. Preserve the refutation and correction of the false printed quantitative estimate. This proves the particular original tube coefficient comparison needed by Federer, without asserting a general mixed-volume foundation. Keep the explicit user omissions and the pending Ward counterexample in 2.10.27.",
